# Spec sources (private capture-log)

SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-or-later

Whenever a file under `tavera/specs/<component>/` cites a source — a Spec
**Sources** entry, an open-item resolution, or an evidence path in a
`debugging-YYYY-MM-DD.md` log — store a durable local copy under the
**private** project-root capture tree (sibling of `source/`, not committed
to the public tree):

```text
capture-log/sources/spec/<component>/
```

`<component>` matches `tavera/specs/<component>/` (for example
`amd64-logical-processors`, `ntfs`).

## Public documents stay silent

Never name `capture-log`, `capture-log/sources`, or this archive layout in
anything committed under `source/` that readers of the public tree see:
`tavera/specs/`, transparency notes that describe sources, README text under
`tavera/`, or other public docs. Agents keep the archive; public citations
name only Learn/`https://` URLs, in-tree paths, `output/` logs with markers,
`tavera/probes/…`, or this project’s GitHub URLs.

Do not put archive copies under `tavera/specs/` or anywhere else that is
committed to the public source repo. Microsoft Learn / OpenSpecs pages may
be stored here as PDF for Ryan’s lookup; they must not enter the public tree.

Every archive artifact must have a matching citation in the public specs
tree (Learn/`https://` URL, in-tree path, `output/` log with marker, or this
project’s GitHub URL). Do not leave an orphan PDF, excerpt, or log in the
private archive with no public citation.

## Layout

```text
capture-log/sources/spec/<component>/
  README.md
  manifest.md
  web/                         # printed PDFs of cited public pages
  intree/                      # excerpts from this checkout
  probes/                      # Spec Sources guest / probe logs
  other/                       # this project's GitHub milestone JSON, etc.
  debugging-YYYY-MM-DD/        # all output/ files for that debugging log
```

The debugging folder name matches the public file
`tavera/specs/<component>/debugging-YYYY-MM-DD.md` (including `-2`, `-3`
suffixes when used).

## What to store

| Kind | Artifact |
|------|----------|
| Public web page | **Print to PDF** (Edge/Chrome `--print-to-pdf`). Human-readable layout required. No scraped plain-text dump as the proof. Record URL and capture date in `manifest.md` and a `.meta.txt` beside the PDF. |
| In-tree code | Short excerpt of the cited symbols/loops. Header must name: path from source root, **commit SHA**, **beginning line number** of each excerpt. |
| Guest / probe log (Spec Sources) | Copy the cited log from `output/` into `probes/` (or DIFF/marker lines). Cite the marker (`DIFF END OK`, etc.) in the **public** spec. Name the probe under `tavera/probes/…`. |
| Debugging-session `output/` | Copy **every** `output/` file the debugging log cites (and every stamp in a cited range that still exists on disk) into `debugging-YYYY-MM-DD/`. Prefer the same basename. Keep probe-tool subfolders when that helps (`probe-v1/…`). Do not archive ISOs, disk images, firmware vars, or built `.exe` unless the log cites them as the evidence itself. |
| This project’s GitHub milestone / issue | JSON or markdown from `gh`. |

When the cited `output/` file still exists, copy it in the same turn as the
citation (or as soon as the run finishes). Refresh the archive copy if the
log on disk is replaced with a newer run that the spec or debugging file
still names.

Keep artifacts small enough to prove the citation. Do not paste proof
bodies into the public spec ([specs.mdc](specs.mdc)).

## Citation in the public specs tree

Public citations name the **real** source only: Learn/OpenSpecs title +
`https://` URL, in-tree path, guest log under `output/` with its marker, or
this project’s GitHub URL. Map Spec Sources entries in the private
`manifest.md`. Debugging archives may use a short private `README.md`
inside `debugging-YYYY-MM-DD/`.

```text
Right: [GetLogicalProcessorInformationEx](https://learn.microsoft.com/…). …
Right: sdk/include/xdk/ketypes.h in this tree. …
Right: output/…/windows-4c1t.log (DIFF END OK); probe tavera/probes/…
Right: public debugging log cites only output/…; agent also copies that file into the private debugging-YYYY-MM-DD/ archive
Wrong: any capture-log path, “private archive”, or manifest.md pointer in tavera/specs/
Wrong: citing only a private PDF as the Sources entry
Wrong: storing Learn PDFs under tavera/specs/
Wrong: scraped text dump instead of a printed PDF in the private archive
Wrong: an in-tree excerpt with no commit SHA or start line
Wrong: citing output/… in a spec or debugging log and leaving no private archive copy when the file still exists
Wrong: a PDF or log in the private archive with no matching public citation
```

## Clean-room

Only allowed sources ([clean-room.mdc](clean-room.mdc),
[clean-room-third-party-sources.mdc](clean-room-third-party-sources.mdc)).
Forbidden pages still must not be opened or stored.

## When a copy cannot be made

Leave the public citation, note “proof missing” in that component’s private
`manifest.md` (or in `debugging-YYYY-MM-DD/README.md` for a debug log), and
tell Ryan which URL or path failed. Do not write “proof missing” about the
private archive into the public spec.
